The project described below will provide an opportunity to use existing plague expertise in Kazakhstan and the U.S. to:
– address important scientific questions;
– provide information that will lead to improved methods for plague prevention and diagnosis; 
– establish long-term collaborative relationships between scientists in Kazakhstan and the U.S. 
The timely application of plague prevention measures depends on our abilities to rapidly recognize human cases and threatening situations, such as plague epizootics in animals. Our ability to effectively target limited plague prevention resources also depends on our understanding of the factors affecting the transmission and maintenance of the plague bacterium…

The objective of proposed project is maintenance, biological and genetic characterization of animal pathogens as well as elaboration of the regional microbial type culture collection of SRAI as a part of the world bank.
Implementation of planned tasks will make it possible:
• to study mechanisms associated with virulence and reactogenicity of viruses; 
• to identify the factors of active effect on a virus genome with a goal to obtain vaccinal strains of higher immunogenicity; 
• to specify the most effective approaches to expansion of cell culture and laboratory animals ranges for large-scale production of viruses.
